From 0218538c0710472ba96ad1619257203cae1d25f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yekai pan <pyk@seas.upenn.edu>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 21:27:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] l2r-local: bug 2 (variant): skip a reused variant cell's
 field store only if the field keeps its offset

Copy avoidance for rc.create_variant (RcCreateFusion,
markVariantAvoidedCopies) skips storing field i of an arm built in a
reused cell when the value is a load of field i of the cell's old arm and
the two arms' member types agree for indices 0..i in declaration order
(hasCompatibleFieldPrefix). That places field i at the same offset only
under the declaration-order layout. The packed record layout, the
default, sorts an arm's members by alignment, so a member's offset depends
on every member of the arm: in `enum M { A(u32, u64), B(u32, u32, u32) }`
A.0 is at offset 8 of the payload and B.0 at offset 0, so building M::B in
a reused M::A cell skipped B.0's store and B.0 read the low half of A.1
(11001 instead of 5001).

Keep the prefix rule and also require field i to sit at the same byte
offset from the box in both: the element starts at the same offset (same
box header shape and element alignment), the arm payload starts at the
same offset within the variant (after the header, at the alignment of the
most aligned arm) and member i at the same offset within the payload.
RecordType::getMemberOffset exposes the packed member offsets from the
derivation the type sizes already use (getElementRegionLayoutInfo now
shares it), which the type converter's LLVM structs follow. The check only
removes skips: reusing a cell for the same arm, arms of the same variant
under --no-pack-record-members, and cells of another variant whose payload
and member offsets agree skip as before.

lean2rr passes --no-pack-record-members because of this bug; its code is
the same with and without this patch (identical LLVM IR for the classic
corpus and a sample of the runtime tests). The structure half of bug 2 is
the earlier local patch (same box type). Test:
tests/integration/conversion/rc_create_fusion_variant_layout.mlir.
